    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog centers on **Cal Raleigh** as our premier start, boasting an elite 75.80 score. Facing a sub-5.00 xERA in Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a favorable spot in the #2 hole, making him our primary source for power production. Outside of our lead catcher, **Tyler Freeman** (59.24) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.46) emerge as high-floor options. **Tyler Freeman** in particular is a tactical play; despite facing the formidable Freddy Peralta, his score is bolstered by a +14% park factor and the potential for a stolen base against a pitcher with a notoriously slow delivery, keeping him firmly in the \"Strong\" category despite the tough matchup. \n\nWe are exercising caution with several players facing elite arms, most notably **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (55.27) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (46.73), both of whom are neutralized by the presence of Paul Skenes and Cole Ragans on the mound. These matchups suppress their raw potential, though **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core piece for his dual-threat capability. The most difficult bench decision today involved **Jeremiah Jackson**, who hovered at a 45.17 score. While his 100% stolen base opportunity against Euclides P\u00e9rez is enticing, the optimizer prioritized the higher-volume plate appearances of our locked-in starters, ultimately keeping **Jeremiah Jackson** on the pine to maintain our daily game cap efficiency.\n\nFinally, owners should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gleyber Torres**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Taylor Ward**. While our projections account for historical batting orders, any shifts downward in the lineup will immediately erode their current scores. We are also wary of **Lawrence Butler** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** facing top-tier velocity; their scores have been adjusted down by 19% to reflect the difficulty of the individual matchups against Wheeler and Ragans, respectively. We are essentially banking on talent over matchup for these core pieces while relying on **Cal Raleigh** and **Tyler Freeman** to drive our offensive output.",
